{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/198474-umbra-the-beginning-nwod-scion","id":198474,"title":"Umbra: the Beginning (nwod+scion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-15T19:42:00-07:00","id":198474,"title":"Umbra: the Beginning (nwod+scion)","content":"I am planning to run a nwod crossover Larp early next year. If it goes well I may keep it going at conventions. I want to incorporate Scion into the mix having the gods be umbral spirits. I know they are not written to go together but that does not mean there isn't room in nwod for it.,Before I go reinventing the wheel I want to see if it has already been done. Should I wait for 2E? what about adapting Scion 2.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","name":"Elroar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3495_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:11:50-07:00","id":199484,"title":"","content":"One Legend 3 Scion with one Sun Boon can wipe out every vampire in a room. One Legend 3 Scion with one Moon Boon can stab a werewolf to death with a pencil that has been enchanted to have all the same effect of a silver weapon. Epic Attributes make a Scion death incarnate against Mages.<br /> <br /> That's the current state of affairs, anyway.<br /> <br /> Don't know if 2E will make things any better or any worse, but I really don't recommend bringing Scions into the World of Darkness. Unless you nerf the HELL out of them, or deny them access to entire Purviews (Sun, Fire, and Moon come to mind) they're going to curbstomp anything else that gets in their way.<br /> <br /> Again, maybe 2E will change things, but I wouldn't count on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T18:58:32-07:00","id":199538,"title":"","content":"Epic Attributes <i>alone</i> make them incredibly unsuitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T20:18:38-07:00","id":199576,"title":"","content":"They would have to be toned down, yes. At a <i>minimum</i>, limit yourself to Heroes. Demigods can easily curbstomp anything short of an Archmaster (and may need some nerfing to avoid doing that, too), and let\u2019s not even get into what Gods can do.<br /> <br /> Setting aside power differentials for the moment, and instead focusing on cosmology and metaphysics:<br /> <br /> I also wouldn\u2019t put them in the Umbra (which doesn\u2019t exist in the nWoD anyway); what <b>Mage</b> calls the Supernal World is a near-perfect match for <b>Scion</b>\u2019s Overworld. I\u2019d equate <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Exarchs with Titan-like beings (who may or may not have once been human), and I\u2019d stick the \u201cWatchtower Realms\u201d of [b]Mage[/i] in or around the former Atlantean Godrealm. Not that it\u2019s likely to matter, as Hero-level Scions rarely traverse Axes Mundi.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d put Tartarus in what nWoD calls the Lower Depths; again, there\u2019s a near-perfect match here. nWoD\u2019s Underworld would merely be one of many, existing alongside the various Pantheons\u2019 Underworlds. If you want, you could say that it\u2019s the Atlantean Underworld; but that might be giving Atlantis\u2019 remnants too much prominence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-16-2014, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T00:48:24-07:00","id":199768,"title":"","content":"Thing is...while placing scions and such in the WoD is a recipe for disaster, you can bring the WoD creatures into scion and they'll fit fine at certain levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T06:45:04-07:00","id":199962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/198474-umbra-the-beginning-nwod-scion?p=199768#post199768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is...while placing scions and such in the WoD is a recipe for disaster, you can bring the WoD creatures into scion and they'll fit fine at certain levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Werewolves and vampires are already in 1E. And in 2E, they're going to get much more development and attention as a valid threat against Scions. 2E will also incorporate the concept of mortal sorcerers who steal power from the Gods.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I think the OP would be well served to not bring Scions into the NWoD at all. Bringing a NWoD-element into the world of Scion, however? Once 2E comes out, that may be more workable.<br /> <br /> But bringing Scions into the NWoD is just a bad idea. Scions outclass pretty much everything. <br /> <br /> Another point I forgot to mention? Mages have to worry about Paradox. Scions don't. They can use their full power anywhere, anytime. Pretty much free of consequences, except for the possibility of Fatebinding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T14:51:00-07:00","id":200418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/198474-umbra-the-beginning-nwod-scion?p=199962#post199962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E will also incorporate the concept of mortal sorcerers who steal power from the Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say what? Link? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T15:55:24-07:00","id":200453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/198474-umbra-the-beginning-nwod-scion?p=200418#post200418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say what? Link? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't seem to find it right now, but it should be on the &quot;What We Know&quot; wiki we've got around here. It's a direct quote from the devs.<br /> <br /> I'm really excited about them, too. I can't wait to see mortals who can actually be relevant against a Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T19:27:06-07:00","id":200660,"title":"","content":"You\u2019ll find it in the thread talking about <b>Scion: Origins</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:13:47-07:00","id":200697,"title":"","content":"I should have gone into more depth of my intentions. First off, yes the players will mainly be playing Scions and the chronicle would end at the demigod/god transition if it goes that far. The games will deal with exploration and research of the various wod cultures to help fight the titans. The inequality of the scions to the rest of the supernatural community will make getting the information even possible as people don't like to share. <br /> <br /> In terms of cosmology and metaphysics I intend to adapt somethings to make it work. Although I will be using nwod mechanics I am swaping in the lore of Mage: the ascension and Hunter: the reckoning. This will help mesh the scion origin story and the implied origin found in exalted so the titians and primordials are the same beings. I am also toying with the idea of having the paradox generated by mages be harmful to heros and demigods due to their dual nature.<br /> <br /> Having the mechanics sync up is a major hurtle. To my ken anything a scion can do is able to be expressed by the structure in nwod as is. I think it would be simpler to adjust Scion in the nwod rules then vice versa. Scions could gain thematically appropriate roates instead of boons based on purview. Knacks would be divided into other learnable rotes and merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","name":"Elroar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3495_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T23:03:00-07:00","id":200760,"title":"","content":"OK: let me see if I understand where you\u2019re coming from. You\u2019re planning to use nWoD rules; but in terms of setting, you\u2019re actually thinking more along the lines of combining <b>Scion</b> with the <i>original</i> World of Darkness \u2014 complete with the notion that <b>Exalted</b> is its prehistory. Right? So what you\u2019re <i>really</i> after is an unholy blend of the <b>Exalted</b>, <b>Scion</b>, and original World of Darkness settings, using the new World of Darkness game engine.<br /> <br /> Are you sure you don\u2019t want to try to squeeze some <b>Adventure!</b> into this too, just to be complete?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T23:50:16-07:00","id":200799,"title":"","content":"I would suggest using the rules for spirit powers in WtF, MtAw or Book of Spirits to simulate purviews and for scions use some of the rules for possessed, but a different nature, their powers coming from spirit <b>heritage </b>and <b>metamorphosis</b>, not possession. Purified (from Immortals) could make pretty good expies for ascended scions or their divine parents with a bit of a power up and tinkering.<br /> <br /> As an aside, years i go i sort of connected some dots in Hunter; the Vigil fluff that lead some interesting setting implications and led to something of a serious Vigil-Scion: Ragnarok crossover/mash-up. Maybe i still have some notes somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-18-2014, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T21:23:40-07:00","id":202631,"title":"","content":"[Vaguely on-topic]<br /> I briefly toyed with the idea of importing Scion's epic attributes into the nWoD... for use with the templates of that game (Read: I did not intend to have the children of gods in my game, rather I wanted an Epic Attribute mechanic for monsters like Werewolves).<br /> I had several ideas, such as alternating target number drop and exploding dice drop for each epic dot, but most of them fell apart at high levels (sort of like Scion 1E does, I suppose). Recently, though, I came up with something that works well.<br /> <br /> Lowering target number is the right way to go with epic attributes to keep them the closest to their original purpose (Mummy the Arisen taught us that). The problem is the ability to have epic attributes go so high! It is best to limit how quickly epics can grow, just like attribute growth is limited. I adopted a one-per-level-of-godhood system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>So here's the system.</b><br /> <br /> At Legend/PowerStat 1, you may purchase up to 1 dot of epic attribute in any attribute. Each dot of epic attribute owned reduces the target number of rolls involving that attribute by 1--so using Strength 3 Epic Strength 1 results in a roll of 3 dice where 7s and up are successes.<br /> For every three additional legend the character accumulates, her maximum number of epic attribute dots increases by one to signify her transition to the next stage of godhood. That is, a Hero has 1 Legend and can go up to Epic 1, a Demigod has 4 Legend and can go up to Epic 2, a God has 7 Legend and can go up to Epic 3, and a Patriarchal God/Matriarchal Goddess (Picture Zeus/Hera) has 10 Legend and can go up to Epic 4. Epic 4 reduces the target number to 4, which is tremendously useful for rolls with that attribute (but doesn't actually increase dice pools in the slightest, that's for regular attributes. Not quite as fantastic as Epic 12 in the Scion system, but you've got to tone things down for nWoD.<br /> <br /> Each dot of epic attribute costs New Dots x 13 (or I suppose New Dots x 11 for the specialty epics; like I said, I wasn't going to use gods for this). Characters can purchase epic attribute dots EVEN IF THE PURCHASE EXCEEDS THE DOTS OWNED IN THE ASSOCIATED ATTRIBUTE. This allows for strange characters that appear inept but have bursts of incredible ability, usually when coupled with Willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like I said, I wasn't intending to actually use Scions with this system, so I don't have anything to say about Boons or Knacks. I just thought it might help to see one of the ways you might handle epics in nWoD.<br /> [/Vaguely on Topic]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [Actually on Topic]<br /> I was in a game where the Storyteller tried to cross Scion with the classic World of Darkness, with Scion being the 'graft' setting. I played a mage, we had one other, one werewolf, two demons, and two Scions. Right around the Demigod line everyone became outpaced by the Scions; the Storyteller tried to fix this by allowing the other templates to purchase epic attributes, but only the mages recovered. The other players wrote themselves out and made new Scion characters to compensate.<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough, as we breached the God transition the mages began to outpace the Scions! Auto successes with attributes, coupled with our storyteller's interpretation of archmastery (which was the 'redirection' of paradox onto other entities) gave the two mages WAY more flexibility than any of the Scions could muster.<br /> <br /> I got a little carried away with it, actually, making an army of squirrel ninjas and trees that grew fully cooked burritos on demand... among other zaney things. He DID make us go insane from the power, though, so I guess that's balance of some sort. For instance, in one scene my mage forgot whether or not he was allergic to bees when one flew into his face. To protect himself from death, he transformed the bee into a bear... because that was the most reasonable response he could muster. Common sense really doesn't apply when you can twist the world into ribbons without personal consequence.<br /> <br /> So it CAN work, but it is going to require some clever footwork on both your part and the part of your players. You have to trust that they will not be as crazy as me. Also, that game's non-Scion characters were using oWoD mechanics, which made them slightly more compatible with the Scion system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}